  enforceMaxStress: 0
  maxAllowedStress: 100
  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 250
  expReward: 75
  offerDialogue:
    name: Reed
    sentences:
    - Another engineer built a bridge at this crossing, but used more material than
      the job needs.
    - Extra members add weight and cost. Some carry the load; others may be doing
      very little.
    - I want you to inspect the design and decide which pieces can come out without
      losing a safe path across.
    - You will have <b><#E09500>Erase, Undo, Redo, and Simulate</color></b>. Remove
      a piece, test the bridge, and restore it if the crossing becomes unsafe.
    - Keep the road intact and get the test vehicle across. Will you take a look?
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Reed
    sentences:
    - The bridge is already in place. Start by studying its members before you erase
      anything.
    - There is no need to draw a new bridge. Find what the structure can do without,
      then run the test.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Reed
    sentences:
    - Find the members the bridge does not need, then test the crossing.
    - If removing one weakens the bridge, use Undo and try a different piece.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Reed
    sentences:
    - The vehicle made it across, and the bridge uses less material now.
    - You identified which pieces could be removed while keeping a working load path.
      Good judgment, {PlayerName}.
